{"findings":[{"rule_id":"WPS-004","evidence":[{"kind":"dimension","ref":"D12","page":1,"quote":"⌀ 16 H7 (+0.018/0)"},{"kind":"title_block","ref":"surface_treatment","page":1,"quote":"I.Z.B.P. (TRIVALENT)"}],"comment":"The ⌀16 H7 bore carries a tight ISO fit tolerance of 0.018 mm, but the drawing does not account for the added thickness of the I.Z.B.P. plating. The plated hole will be undersize and may reject the mating shaft; the designer should reduce the pre-plate bore size or add a note specifying reaming after plating."
  ,
"recommended_correction":"Reduce the pre-plate bore limits to allow for plating build-up, or add a note requiring the hole to be reamed to final size after plating."}]}
